{"text": "SIERRA VISTA IMMIGRATION LAW GROUP, P.C. -- CASE NOTES\nMatter: 26-IMM-0291   Atty: S. Ibarra-Whitcomb   Portal:\nhttps://portal.sierravistalaw.example/c/26-IMM-0291\n\nBENEFICIARY: TRAN, Minh Khoi (passport spelling) / Trần Minh Khôi\n   goes by \"Khoi\"\n   DOB: 22 Feb 1994, Đà Nẵng, Vietnam\n   A-number: A 216 448 907\n   Passport: C4471882 (Vietnam), exp. 11 Aug 2029\n   I-94 no.: 73018845521\n   ITIN: 953-78-4410 (no SSN yet)\nPETITIONER / SPOUSE: Chase Abernethy, U.S. citizen by birth\n   DOB 1991-07-30, SSN 667 37 3167\nHome (both): 745 Lincoln Ave, Unit 12, San Jose, CA 95126\nKhoi cell 408.555.0171   Chase cell +1 408 555 0109\nEmail: khoi.tran94@mail.example; c.abernethy@southbayfab.example (Chase's work, AVOID)\n\n1/14/2026 - INITIAL CONSULT (SIW)\nKhoi entered at SFO on 08/17/2018 in F-1 status to attend De Anza Community College.\nStopped attending spring 2020 when his father (Trần Văn Hùng) became ill and money\nran out; SEVIS terminated 06/02/2020. So: out of status since June 2020, but\ninspected and admitted -> eligible to adjust under INA § 245(a) as immediate\nrelative. Unauthorized employment forgiven for IRs. He has been working the line at a\nrestaurant owned by Pho Hoa Binh Restaurant Group LLC, paid by check, files with the ITIN.\nMarried Chase October 4, 2025 at the Santa Clara County Clerk-Recorder; reception\nat his parents' place in Los Gatos. This is a same-sex marriage; Khoi says\nhis family in Vietnam does not know and asked that nothing be mailed there.\nISSUE: one arrest. 3/9/2021, petty theft (Cal. Penal Code § 484), Santa Clara\nCounty Superior Court docket C2104417. Completed diversion, dismissed 9/21/2021. Need\ncertified disposition. Not a CIMT problem w/ petty offense exception but must disclose.\nQuoted flat fee $4,800 + filing fees ($1,440 I-485, $675 I-130). Chase paid\nretainer $2,400 by card ending 8493.\n\n2/3/2026 - DOCS RECEIVED\nJoint lease; joint acct at South Bay Federal Credit Union (acct 0098314472, opened 11/12/2025);\nwedding photos; Chase's 2024 return (AGI $96,410) for Form I-864.\nMissing: Khoi's birth cert translation; school transcripts.\n\n2/19/2026 - MEDICAL\nI-693 done by civil surgeon Dr. Anand Krishnamurthy, Willow Glen Urgent & Occupational Care.\nIGRA positive, chest x-ray clear -> latent TB. Started rifampin 600 mg daily x 4 months.\nDr. K says this is Class B, not a bar. Vaccines complete.\n\n3/2/2026 - FILED concurrent I-130 / I-485 / I-765. Receipts:\n   I-130  IOE0926114478\n   I-485  IOE0926114479\n   I-765  IOE0926114480\nClient set up his own USCIS online account -- login khoitran_sj / pw Banhmi#2018! (he\nemailed it to us; told him to change it and NOT to send passwords by email).\n\n4/27/2026 - Biometrics done at ASC, 122 Charcot Ave. Interview notice came:\nJuly 16, 2026, 8:15 am, USCIS San Jose Field Office. Prep session w/ both\nspouses set for 7/9/2026. Remind Mr. Abernethy to bring original birth\ncertificate. Soledad Ibarra-Whitcomb to attend.", "kind": "Text file", "detail": "451 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Minh Khoi", "Chase Abernethy", "Trần Văn Hùng", "Dr. Anand Krishnamurthy", "khoitran"], "companies": ["SIERRA VISTA IMMIGRATION LAW GROUP, P.C.", "Pho Hoa Binh Restaurant Group LLC", "South Bay Federal Credit Union", "Southbayfab", "Willow Glen Urgent & Occupational Care", "USCIS San Jose Field Office"]}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.2999999988824129, "modelMs": 30948.5, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "passport_dl", "routing", "phone", "record", "vin", "account", "money", "dob", "age90", "date", "street", "zip", "postal_ca", "names"], "detections": [{"start": 0, "end": 40, "text": "SIERRA VISTA IMMIGRATION LAW GROUP, P.C.", "kind": "company", "source": "model", "canonical": "SIERRA VISTA IMMIGRATION LAW GROUP, P.C."}, {"start": 63, "end": 74, "text": "26-IMM-0291", "kind": "record", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "26-IMM-0291"}